\ Wide equal-choice reference vectors computed with exact decimal arithmetic.
\ These test both directions, wrapped digits, rejection, and k=3.
\ Inputs are ordinary decimal text; no CAL native integer carries them.
\ The CAL compiler has not yet run these checks.

To check the two digit forward choice:
  Put "170141183460469231731687303715884105727" into the seal inquiry's starting answer.
  Put 1 into the seal inquiry's answer direction.
  Put "170141183460469231731687303715884105728" into a requested options wide quantity.
  Choose an equal option given the requested options wide quantity.
  If the wide option work's digit count is not 2,
    put "The two digit forward choice used the wrong digit count." into the check report; exit.
  If the wide option work's period is not "28948022309329048855892746252171976962977213799489202546401021394546514198529",
    put "The two digit forward choice used the wrong M power." into the check report; exit.
  If the wide option work's acceptance limit is not "28948022309329048855892746252171976962977213799489202546401021394546514198528",
    put "The two digit forward choice computed the wrong acceptance limit." into the check report; exit.
  If the wide option work's constructed answer is not "170141183460469231731687303715884105727",
    put "The two digit forward choice built the wrong wide value." into the check report; exit.
  If the seal inquiry's selected quantity is not "170141183460469231731687303715884105727",
    put "The two digit forward choice chose the wrong option." into the check report; exit.
  If the seal inquiry's current answer is not the seal inquiry's starting answer,
    put "The two digit forward choice changed the stream cursor." into the check report; exit.

